{"created": "2026-07-29T20:28:25.867618+00:00", "modified": "2026-07-30T20:15:02.947025+00:00", "id": 21689760, "conceptrecid": "21671567", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21689760", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21671567", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21689760", "metadata": {"title": "Coherent-State Circuit Cancellation and the Compact-Group Mathieu Conjecture", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21689760", "publication_date": "2026-07-20", "description": "<div>\n<div>We prove that the Mathieu conjecture for a compact connected Lie group holds if and only if the group is a torus. Equivalently, for every nonabelian compact connected Lie group we construct finite-type functions whose pure Haar moments vanish at every positive order while fixed mixed moments remain nonzero. A coherent-state moment identity treats every adjoint simple group of rank at least two, an explicit circuit treats SO(3), and passage to simple adjoint quotients covers all exceptional types, central quotients, half-spin groups, nonstandard global forms, products, and torus factors. We further determine the exact disconnected boundary. If the identity component is an r-dimensional torus and the group has N components, its finite-type function algebra with Haar integration is equivalent to the identity-coefficient functional on C[Z^r x C_N]; hence the remaining virtually toral problem depends only on (r,N). The paper also proves a general phase-invariant circuit criterion, a four-term Gaussian counterexample family, and degree-three support minimality.</div>\n</div>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Liu, Zongmin", "affiliation": "Stanford University", "orcid": "0000-0003-2720-8170"}], "keywords": ["Mathieu conjecture", "Gaussian Moments Conjecture", "compact Lie groups", "sphere-transitive representations", "Mathieu-Zhao subspaces", "central quotients", "radial moments", "Gaussian moments", "compact connected Lie groups", "highest-weight representations", "coherent states", "Haar integration"], "version": "2.2", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 2, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "21671567"}}]}}, "title": "Coherent-State Circuit Cancellation and the Compact-Group Mathieu Conjecture", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21689760", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21689760", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21689760?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21689760", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21689760", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21689760", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21689760/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21671567", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21671567", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21671567", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21671567", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21689760/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21689760/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21689760/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21689760/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21689760:coherent_state_mathieu_classification_v2.2.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21689760:coherent_state_mathieu_classification_v2.2.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21689760:coherent_state_mathieu_classification_v2.2.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21689760:coherent_state_mathieu_classification_v2.2.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21689760:coherent_state_mathieu_classification_v2.2.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/ii